MLLM description: The English Setter is a medium-sized dog with a distinctive long, silky coat that can come in various colors and patterns, including liver and white, black and white, and roan. Its head is broad with a flat top, and it has a long, narrow muzzle. The eyes are almond-shaped and dark, giving the dog an alert expression. The ears are long, hanging down close to the cheeks, and they are often covered with long hair.

In terms of size and proportions, the English Setter is typically between 22-27 inches tall at the shoulder and weighs around 50-65 pounds. They have a strong, muscular build with a deep chest and a slightly arched back. Their tail is long and feathered, adding to their elegant appearance.

Behaviorally, English Setters are known for their friendly, gentle, and affectionate nature. They are highly intelligent and make excellent hunting dogs due to their keen sense of smell and ability to retrieve game. They are also good with children and other pets, making them great family companions.

Unique identifying traits include their long, silky coat, which requires regular grooming to maintain its health and appearance. Additionally, their distinctive head shape and long, feathered tail set them apart from other breeds.
